==English==

===Etymology 1===
Derives from the height of {{w|Oliver R. Smoot}}, who had lain on the Harvard Bridge to measure it as a fraternity prank at MIT.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|smo͞ot}}
* {{IPA|en|/smuːt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-smoot.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːt|s=1}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|humorous|chiefly|Greater Boston}} A [[unit]] of [[length]] defined as exactly sixty-seven [[inch|inches]] (approximately 1.70 [[meter|meters]]).

