* {{pedia}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|*smote}}, {{m|enm|*smotte}}, from {{der|en|non|smátta|t=narrow passageway, gap}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*smēhtǭ|t=narrow path}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*smēhaz|t=small, narrow}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|smoat|smout|smeut|smot|smut|smute|smeyut}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|British|dialectal}} A small opening built into a [[dry-stone]] wall, fence, or hedge to allow sheep (and hares) to pass through; a [[thirl]].

